00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.440
are we to make errors if you look at professional&nbsp;
software developers on their first submission of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:27.520
code they across studies make anywhere from&nbsp;
150 errors per thousand of lines of code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.440
so how many errors do we think we make as amateur&nbsp;
software developers um and how likely are they to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:39.520
impact our scientific conclusions well we know&nbsp;
of examples where this has happened um one comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.600
from the work of jeffrey chang he was a structural&nbsp;
biologist who published a bunch of papers in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:52.560
early 2000s about this particular protein the&nbsp;
